  "uT": 1.0,
  "summary": "Murphy's 20-minute frontal session, which the vendor offers against 'lethargy, listlessness or mental fogginess' after too much temporal-lobe or one-sided stimulation. Hippocampal and amygdala signals run one after the other from static coils over both eyes with opposite polarity; the vendor states it 'treats both sides of the brain the same'.",
  "setting": "Only as needed after over-stimulation; the vendor asks users to contact tech support first. Four coils on the forehead: Fp1 and AF3 above the left eye, Fp2 and AF4 above the right eye; the other four coils stay unused.",
  "schedule": "One 20-minute run; the vendor says it 'can be run twice, if necessary', and not three times.",
  "notes": "The vendor says to use 'only two or four coils', with opposite polarities, 'one or two coils over each eye'. Here the left pair (Fp1, AF3) gets the signal and the right pair (Fp2, AF4) the same signal reversed (weight -1); splitting the polarity by side is a project reading. For the two-coil form, unplug AF3 and AF4. The coils stay still, with no rotation. Approximations: the hippocampal 'LTP' and amygdala 'burstx' templates are proprietary. Each 9.5-s cycle follows the vendor's 'one after the other ... with a four-second latency' and its standard 3-ms points: five hippocampal theta bursts at 5 Hz (about 0.84 s; each 4 biphasic pulses at about 110 Hz, the nearest the 3-ms grid allows to the 100 Hz of the project's ltp generator; the number of bursts is a project choice), 4 s of silence, the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz) for 230 points of 3 ms (0.69 s, the published burst-firing length), then 4 s of silence. That gives about 9.6 s of field per minute, the vendor's figure for its standard signals; the same stand-in is used in murphy-paranormal-shakti-frontal. Do not exceed two runs; stop on distress. Not for people with epilepsy or a psychiatric condition. This session rests on vendor statements only and is not a treatment for anything. Independent double-blind tests of the related temporal-lobe sessions found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012).",
  "targets": ["vmpfc", "left-dlpfc", "right-dlpfc"],
